# Security Director Rule (`security-governance`, v1.2.0)

1. Execute `python3 .cursor/skills/security-director/tools/sec_cpu_scanner.py --root . --format json` and normalize Tier B SARIF (`semgrep`, `gitleaks`, `osv-scanner`, `trivy`) via `sarif_ingest.py` before semantic review.
2. Fail closed if any required scanner is missing (`UNVERIFIED_MISSING_TOOL`, cap verdict at `ITERATE`).
3. Load only active `.cursor/skills/security-director/references/modules/<slug>/BRIEF.md` briefs matching `control-matrix.yaml` (`<= 25,600 B`).
4. Run Clean-Room cross-model auditors (`auditor-authz-intent`, `auditor-agentic-abuse`) without builder chain-of-thought and terminate with `Verdict Envelope v1.2.0`.
